-- R12 - prediction-market odds (Polymarket, Kalshi) as what's-priced evidence in both Macro Takeaways digests.
-- Owner ask, 28 Oct 2026 (project thread "Add prediction market odds to takeaways"). Data: scripts/predmkt/predmkt.py,
-- run daily 06:38 SGT by the scheduled task "Prediction-market odds daily refresh"; Drive file predmkt_latest.
-- Proposed with this exact statement (dash.propose_rule; apply_after = next Sunday 20:00 SGT unless "oppose R12").
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R12' and status = 'proposed';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Prediction-market odds (Polymarket, Kalshi) as what's-priced evidence next to R02 positioning and the not-already-priced gate", "body": "PREDICTION MARKETS RULE (owner, 28 Oct 2026). At the evidence step, in the same pass as R02 positioning and R04 attention, open the Google Drive plain-text file titled predmkt_latest (Drive search_files with title = 'predmkt_latest', take the newest match, then read_file_content). It is refreshed about 06:40 SGT from the public Polymarket and Kalshi APIs: open macro contracts (central-bank decisions, US CPI / core CPI / unemployment / payrolls / GDP ladders with an implied median, recession, oil and gold hit-price contracts, Hormuz / Iran / Israel / Russia-Ukraine geopolitics, elections), each with p = crowd-implied probability, d1/d7 = change in percentage points, 24h volume and liquidity or open interest. If the file is missing or its header date is more than 2 days old, print 'PM odds: stale' and skip this rule. It is evidence about what the crowd prices, never a directional view, and has no tested read (R03): it never raises p by itself.\n\n1. WHAT'S PRICED. For each theme and each NEW card whose catalyst is a listed contract (the meeting, the release, the dated geopolitical outcome, the oil/gold level), print one clause: 'PM odds: <contract> <p> (d7 <+/-x>pp, <venue>)'. For data ladders quote the implied median, e.g. 'PM odds: Oct core CPI implied median 0.18% m/m, P(>0.3) 16%'.\n2. NOT-ALREADY-PRICED GATE. When a card's thesis needs an outcome the crowd already puts at 80% or more (or the opposite at 20% or less), say so in the card's case against ('PM: outcome ~85% priced') and the card must rest on the residual: the surprise versus the implied median, the tail, or a second-order effect. A card that only restates a >=80% contract fails the gate.\n3. GAP CHECK. Where the digest has the rates- or options-implied odds for the same meeting (OIS / fed funds futures, CME FedWatch style) or the survey consensus for the same print, compare. Print 'PM gap: <contract> PM <p> vs <market/consensus> <q>' when the decision odds differ by 10pp or more, or a ladder median differs from consensus by at least 0.1pp (CPI m/m, unemployment), 0.2pp (CPI y/y, GDP q/q saar) or 50k (payrolls). A gap is a question to check (which side is thin, stale or reading the contract wording differently), not a signal; name the likelier explanation in one clause.\n4. MOVES. A d7 move of 15pp or more on a contract tied to an open card or a live theme goes in the BOOK CHECK line as evidence the crowd has moved toward or away from the card.\n5. FILTERS. Ignore contracts with 24h volume under $5k and liquidity/open interest under $50k, ladders whose P(above) is not monotone, and contracts resolving within 24 hours of the digest unless the event is today. Read Polymarket titles literally: geopolitical contracts resolve on specific wording.\n\nFOOTER: one line 'Prediction markets: <n> contracts cited; gaps: <list or none>; file <header date>'.", "rationale": "Owner, 28 Oct 2026, after the Bloomberg report that Millennium PMs are building tools on Polymarket/Kalshi data: use prediction-market odds in the Macro Takeaways workflow. The cheap, defensible use is as a what's-priced and crowd input next to positioning (R02) and the spec's not-already-priced gate, plus a gap check against rates- and survey-implied odds, without treating the odds as a forecast.", "evidence": "Daily file built by scripts/predmkt/predmkt.py (public Polymarket Gamma API and Kalshi trade API, no keys) into project files predmkt/ and the Drive digest folder; first pull 28 Oct 2026: about 45 Polymarket and 33 Kalshi macro events, 13 KB. Daily history accumulates in predmkt_daily.csv for a later test of whether PM moves or PM-vs-rates gaps lead anything; no predictive test yet.", "revert_if": "Revert or revise if by 30 Nov 2026 no card or theme was changed by a PM line (dead weight), or if two or more 'PM gap' flags turn out to be contract-wording or stale-price artefacts in a week.", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2026-11-30", "source": "owner"}$j$::jsonb);
